plugin-hostd (0.15.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.15.9: the binary and the manual pages say 0.15.9
  * Release 0.15.9: a plugin that changes a callee-saved register runs alone
    (#366)
  * relay: the supervisor takes the abi_clobber reports the relay thread read
    and never reads a worker itself; the abi line parsed with isdigit, the
    fuzz records at the lines that moved
  * the omx-clap-core vocabulary as the channel's omx-contract 3.6.0 renders
    it
  * omx-clap-core 0.26.2: its vocabulary rendered again, and the floor where
    the abi_clobber event comes from
  * fuzz: the records name relay.c's lines as they are now
  * fuzz: the reply-no-loss-read mutant applies to relay_remove as it is now
  * tests: the fake host reads abi_clobber from its declaration
  * tests: an abi_clobber report of a removed instance leaves nothing for a
    new instance that reuses its number
  * docs: the protocol page lists the abi_clobber event
  * relay: shutdown frees each source's list of abi_clobber reports
  * relay: abi_clobber reports kept without a cap, once each, purged when the
    instance goes; the tick acts only while the instance is on the worker
    that wrote it
  * tests: twenty abi_clobber reports in one burst are all acted on, and a
    chain member leaves its chain; the fake's abi_clobber_all, red
  * supervisor: a worker's abi_clobber quarantines the instance and moves it
    to a worker of its own with its state when it shares one; the relay keeps
    the instance for the tick
  * tests: a member whose worker says abi_clobber leaves its pool for a
    worker of its own with its state; one alone is only marked, red

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 00:55:59 +0000
